  "Question": "If \\(a,\\) \\(b,\\) \\(c\\) are nonzero real numbers such that \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac{a+b-c}{c} &=\\frac{a-b+c}{b}\\\\ &=\\frac{-a+b+c}{a}, \\end{aligned} \\] and \\[ x=\\frac{(a+b)(b+c)(c+a)}{abc}, \\] and \\(x\\lt0,\\) then \\(x\\) equals",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(-1\\)",
    "B": "\\(-2\\)",
    "C": "\\(-4\\)",
    "D": "\\(-6\\)",
    "E": "\\(-8\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "A",
  "Solution": "Each numerator differs from \\(a+b+c\\) by twice its denominator. This suggests defining \\(S=a+b+c\\). Since \\(a,b,c\\) are nonzero, the given fractions can be rewritten as\n\\[\n\\frac Sc-2=\\frac Sb-2=\\frac Sa-2.\n\\]\nAdding 2 gives\n\\[\n\\frac Sc=\\frac Sb=\\frac Sa.\n\\]\nIf \\(S\\ne0\\), we may divide by \\(S\\), obtaining \\(1/c=1/b=1/a\\). Thus \\(a=b=c\\), and\n\\[\nx=\\frac{(2a)(2a)(2a)}{a^3}=8.\n\\]\nThis contradicts \\(x<0\\), so \\(S=0\\).\n\nNow \\(a+b=-c\\), \\(b+c=-a\\), and \\(c+a=-b\\). Therefore\n\\[\nx=\\frac{(-c)(-a)(-b)}{abc}=-1,\n\\]\nwhere cancellation is valid because \\(abc\\ne0\\). The answer is \\(-1\\), choice \\(\\mathrm{A}\\).",
